Package: openstack-net-attach
Version: 1.1.4
Section: net
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Depends: systemd, iproute2
Recommends: isc-dhcp-client
Maintainer: Coredge Team <yesveer@coredge.io>
Description: OpenStack Network Hot-plug Manager for Ubuntu
 Automatically detects and configures network interfaces that are
 hot-plugged into OpenStack virtual machines after initial boot.
 .
 When OpenStack attaches a new network to a running VM, the kernel
 creates a new interface but Ubuntu does not configure it by default.
 This daemon monitors netlink events and runs DHCP on every new
 interface as soon as it appears — no reboot required.
 .
 Supports systemd-networkd (default) and dhclient backends.
 Installs as a systemd service that starts automatically on boot.
Installed-Size: 3108
